            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks like a platform specific thing.\n\nDo you think it makes sense to put a meson option for this purpose?\n\nsomething like \n\n`-Dhost-powerstate-change-timeout=20`\n`-Dhost-powerstate-change-retry=3`\n\nor just the timeout and then leave the retry as hardcoded.\n\nOtherwise we are taking a 1 minute delay for the update logic even on platforms which do not take so long, extending the time until the user gets an error for a failed update."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "I don\u2019t think we are actually taking 1 minute delay if the expected state is reached earlier. For example, if the state is achieved within 5 seconds, the update will proceed after just 5 seconds.\n\nI agree we could add a Meson option `host-powerstate-change-timeout` for the timeout, but 12 seconds seems too short for a graceful power-off on most platforms. We could increase the default timeout to 30 or even 60 seconds."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/host_power.cpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com Lets add a meson option with default value of 20. Name it something like -\n\nhost-state-transition-timeout\n\nIn the description please mention that this option is being used in bios-software-update service to control the host state transition timeout when a host is turned off & on, before & after a bios update. Please fix the verbatim accordingly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/host_power.cpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Done."
                }
            ],
